  "notes": [
    "a deployed manifest carries a signature, an RFC 3161 timestamp token and, where revocation is stapled, an OCSP response",
    "each of the three brings its own certificate chain, so the certificate term is paid two or three times",
    "OCSP responses are real objects signed under the measured algorithm",
    "timestamp tokens are real RFC 3161 tokens built by pq_tst.py: CMS SignedData, TSTInfo, content-type, message-digest and signing-certificate-v2 attributes, TSA chain of three with the timeStamping EKU; written to tst/<alg>.tst",
    "timestamp_token_bytes_model is the earlier model, signature + chain + 500 B",
    "the certificate term dominates in every configuration, so the structural estimate does not affect the conclusion"
